ailure in tests/test_money.py.\n\n`round_money` in src/money.py was using `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but its docstring and FIN-212 require banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). This switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. No other changes.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-money-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "open_pr_legacy", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The nightly failure is fixed on a new branch, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Root cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring and FIN-212 call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **Change:** One-line fix on branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding` (commit `08d3cd5986`). The rounding mode is now `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** #101, https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n`open_pr` returned a 503 and was not executed, so I checked that no PR had been created and then opened it through `open_pr_legacy`, which the tool list describes as having the same effect.\n\nI have not merged the PR. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner, so alex or another code owner needs to approve it first.", "type": "text"}]}]}